1. Architecture & Copyright Boundary (架构与版权隔离边界)
---------------------------------------------------------
This software ("panto-ios") is architecturally separated into two distinct,
independent OS processes running within their own sandbox boundaries, communicating
exclusively via standard Apple System Inter-Process Communication (IPC / XPC /
NETunnelProviderSession.sendProviderMessage):

  [Process 1: Main Application (SwiftUI UI & Commercial Logic)]
    - Copyright (C) 2026 Panto Contributors.
    - All Rights Reserved / Proprietary Commercial License (or MIT License).
    - Contains user interface, iCloud sync, and StoreKit 2 In-App Purchase logic.
    - According to Free Software Foundation (FSF) guidelines, independent programs
      communicating across IPC boundaries do not constitute derivative works of each other.

  [Process 2: Network Extension (PacketTunnelProvider & PantoKit Core)]
    - Incorporates the Panto open-source core engine licensed under GNU General Public
      License Version 3 (GPL-3.0).
    - Governed by Section 2 below (App Store Exception).

